@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Launch environment — what the agent must already hold when sbx starts it

' purpose: why everything the agent needs AT LAUNCH is rendered host-side into the kit environment, and what that environment carries
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (launchEnv, launchConfigEnv, gitSafeDirectoryEnv, scopedGitIndexEnv, startupCommands)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/launch_config_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/own_agent_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/kit.go (SeedEntrypointCommand)
' covers: cmd/proveo/testdata/plan/sbx-claudecode-broker.golden
' covers: cmd/proveo/testdata/plan/sbx-claudecode-shell-clone-datadir.golden
' covers: cmd/proveo/testdata/plan/sbx-cursor-key.golden
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' Siblings, so this one stays about the LAUNCH INSTANT:
'   the backend that builds it ..... _spec/internal/sbx/sandbox-backend.puml
'   the Kit's three work kinds ..... _spec/internal/sbx/sbx-kit-contract.puml
'   the seed's own step order ...... _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml
'   one canonical host path ........ _spec/internal/workspace/subdir-scope-mounts.puml
'
' ── MEASURED: THE KIT'S STARTUP COMMANDS DO NOT GATE THE AGENT LAUNCH ──────
' Measured 2026-09-15/16, sbx 0.42.1, on the development host: the interactive
' shell is handed over at t≈0, and the kit dispatcher reports `dispatcher
' complete` at t+15–30s. Nothing in the Kit schema can change that ordering —
' `KitCommand` is command/user/description and offers no blocking form, so
' there is no way to ask sbx to wait for a startup command before it launches.
'
' Two consequences, and they are different in kind:
'   an EXPORT   never arrives. A setup command runs in its own process, so a
'               variable it exports reaches nothing the agent inherits. This
'               was already the rule (sbx-kit-contract.puml, env-shaped work);
'               the measurement says only that it is not a near miss.
'   a WRITE     arrives LATE. Files do outlive the command that wrote them, but
'               a one-shot run (`-p "prompt"`, `run <task>`) can be finished
'               before the write lands, so file-shaped work is safe only for a
'               session the operator keeps driving.
'
' ── THE RULE THIS LEAVES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Anything the agent must HOLD at launch — its environment, its config file,
' its git index, the repository's safety — is proveo's to resolve HOST-SIDE and
' render into the kit environment. Anything that may legitimately happen AFTER
' launch — seed composition, house rules, toolchain provisioning — may stay a
' startup command. `launchEnv` is the first half of that rule made concrete.
'
' ── WHAT launchEnv CARRIES, AND WHY EACH ITEM CANNOT WAIT ──────────────────
'   the plan's own env            egress.AgentEnv, filtered (sandbox-backend.puml)
'   PROVEO_WORKDIR                the mount's HOST path; sbx has no -w
'   GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILE…=1  each virtiofs workspace is its OWN filesystem
'                                 and git will not walk up across one, so a
'                                 scope mounted beside its .git finds no repo.
'   GIT_CONFIG_COUNT / KEY_0 /    git refuses the repository root it is then
'   VALUE_0 = safe.directory      shown, for dubious ownership. The docker
'                                 entrypoint exports the same three in-process;
'                                 under sbx that process is not the agent's.
'   OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT       opencode selects its model from its CONFIG
'   OPENCODE_MODEL / _SMALL_MODEL file, not from OPENAI_* env. The inline JSON
'                                 mirrors configure_opencode_local_model in
'                                 defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh, and was measured
'                                 against the image: with it set, `opencode
'                                 models` lists the local ollama/<model>.
'   GIT_INDEX_FILE                the scoped index, below.
'
' The root handed to safe.directory is EvalSymlinks'd for the same reason the
' mounts are: one spelling, or the declaration names a path git never sees.
'
' ── THE SCOPED INDEX IS BUILT ON THE HOST ──────────────────────────────────
' A subproject scope mounts the scope and a few siblings, so every OTHER tracked
' path is absent inside the sandbox and `git status` reports the repository as
' mostly deleted. The docker entrypoint answers this in-process: copy .git/index,
' mark every tracked path that is not present skip-worktree, export
' GIT_INDEX_FILE. Under sbx the export would die with the startup command, so
' the same index is built HOST-SIDE instead — index entries are worktree-RELATIVE,
' which is what makes the file portable — written under the mounted proveo home
' at git-index/<sid>, and named in the environment the agent starts with. The
' host's own .git is never touched: the copy is what `update-index` is pointed at.
'
' ── THE MIXIN'S THIRD STARTUP COMMAND ──────────────────────────────────────
' `startupCommands` appends `/usr/bin/env PROVEO_SEED_ONLY=1 /entrypoint.sh` for
' a mixin kit only; a `kind: sandbox` kit declares the image's own ENTRYPOINT as
' its process prefix and needs no such command. PROVEO_SEED_ONLY makes
' `proveo_exec_agent` return instead of exec — the script is wanted for its
' wiring, and the agent sbx launched is the only one that may exist.
' The kit ENVIRONMENT is deliberately identical between the two kinds, which is
' what `own_agent_test.go` asserts — it compares the two setups with exactly that
' one command removed.
'
' SETTLED 2026-09-16 — it is the ONLY run, not a second one. The question was
' whether the def entrypoint ALSO runs as the container's process prefix under a
' mixin. It does not, measured three ways on sbx v0.42.1 (target opencode):
'   · before the seed-only command existed, a sandbox probed after `dispatcher
'     complete` held opencode.json with `"provider": {}` and an EMPTY
'     $OPENCODE_MODEL — configure_opencode_local_model had run nowhere.
'   · Promptful's transcript reached `> build …` and `Error: Invalid API Key`
'     with no `🚀 Launching opencode` line, which the def echoes immediately
'     before proveo_exec_agent.
'   · with the command in place, that launch line and `🌱 seed-only: …` appear
'     ONLY under 002-startup-opencode-posture/001-cmd.sh in
'     /var/log/sbx-kit-startup.log, and opencode.json then carries
'     provider.ollama.
' The deciding factor is which Kit supplies the `sandbox:` block: a mixin leaves
' it to sbx's built-in agent, whose command replaces the image's entrypoint. The
' kind-by-kind account is in _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml, which this
' measurement corrected. Nothing above changes — the rule is about what a startup
' command cannot deliver in time — but the stakes do: for a mixin this command is
' the def's ONLY chance to run, so anything dropped from it is dropped outright.

component """sandbox.Spec"" → ""launchEnv""\nresolved HOST-side, before the run" as LE <<app>>
component "kit ""environment.variables""\nwhat the agent inherits" as ENV <<app>>
component "kit ""setup.startup""\n""proveo-seed"" · seed-only entrypoint" as SU <<app>>

component "agent session\nshell handed over at t≈0" as AG <<app>>
component """dispatcher complete""\nt+15–30s, after the agent" as DISP <<error>>

component "git reach + safety\n""GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILESYSTEM""\n""safe.directory"" as GIT_CONFIG_*" as GITENV <<app>>
component "opencode model wiring\n""OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT""" as OC <<app>>
database "scoped index\n<proveo home>/git-index/<sid>" as IDX <<db>>

LE ARROW_MAIN ENV
ENV ARROW_MAIN AG : held at the first instruction
LE ARROW_MAIN GITENV
LE ARROW_MAIN OC
LE ARROW_MAIN IDX : built on the host, named in the env
SU ARROW_QUEUE DISP
DISP ARROW_ERROR AG : too late for anything the agent holds

note bottom of DISP
  **Startup commands do not gate the launch.**
  sbx hands the shell over immediately, while the
  kit dispatcher reports completion 15 to 30
  seconds later, so an export written there
  reaches a process the agent already started.
end note

note bottom of LE
  **The rule the race leaves.** Whatever the
  agent must already hold — its environment, its
  config, its index — proveo renders host-side
  into the kit; whatever may land afterwards can
  stay a startup command.
end note

note right of GITENV
  **Git needs two facts before it will look.**
  Each virtiofs workspace is its own filesystem,
  so discovery must be told to cross one, and the
  synthesised root is refused for dubious
  ownership until safe.directory declares it.
end note

note right of OC
  **opencode reads its model from a file, not
  from the environment.** So the wiring travels
  as an inline config in OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT,
  merged at start — measured against the image,
  which then lists the local model as its own.
end note

note bottom of IDX
  **The index is built on the host and named in
  the environment.** Index entries are worktree
  relative, so the copy relocates intact; the
  host repository is never touched, and every
  tracked path no mount covers is skip-worktree.
end note

note bottom of SU
  **A mixin kit gets a third startup command.**
  PROVEO_SEED_ONLY makes proveo_exec_agent return
  instead of exec, so the def's own wiring runs
  while the kit environment stays identical
  between the two kinds.
end note

note right of AG
  **A write is late rather than lost.** Files
  outlive the command that produced them, so
  composition may remain a startup step, while
  anything a one-shot instruction must already
  hold is resolved before the agent launches.
end note
@enduml
